Phasmid: system font (Windows profiles)

What:     For a windows profile, system-ui is the Windows menu font: Segoe UI,
          or by the first of locale.languages Yu Gothic UI (ja), Microsoft
          YaHei UI (zh-CN), Microsoft JhengHei UI (zh-TW, HK, MO, Hant) or
          Malgun Gothic (ko). The CSS keywords menu, small-caption and
          status-bar use it at 12 px; the other keywords stay Arial at the
          default size, as in layout_theme_font_provider_win.cc. Linux
          profiles are unchanged.
Why:      Linux Chrome sends the GTK UI font as system-ui and answers every
          system font keyword with Arial.
Profile:  os.family, locale.languages
Hooks:    content/browser/renderer_host/render_view_host_impl.cc
          RenderViewHostImpl::GetPlatformSpecificPrefs;
          third_party/blink/renderer/core/layout/
          layout_theme_font_provider_default.cc
          LayoutThemeFontProvider::SystemFontFamily, SystemFontSize
Contexts: main, iframes and workers of a page's renderer; a worker-only
          process has no system font family, as in stock.
Guard:    tests/guards/fonts/windows_metrics.py

